s, btoa, RFC1924/git b85, Z85, IPv6 RFC1924, a85 over a seen inner layer\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Most likely D24 (knob on D23 Adobe Ascii85 '<~...~>'). Build warmups_codecs.b85_any(t): strip whitespace/newlines; '<~..~>' -> a85decode(adobe=True) (append '~>' if only '<~' present); else a85decode(t) (z = 4 NULs) and a85decode(t, foldspaces=True) (y); b85decode (RFC1924/git/Python alphabet); Z85 via str.translate(Z85 alphabet -> b85 alphabet) then b85decode (pad to len%5==0 only for b85-style partials); btoa: lines between 'xbtoa Begin' and 'xbtoa End', a85 per line; IPv6 RFC1924 = 20-char token -> 16 bytes. Then magic sniff (gzip/zlib/bz2/xz/raw deflate) and decode_chunk on the output (hex/UTF-16/base64 inner layers), slug-gated. Register as a whole-blob candidate AND a free codec for 7-12 char Mastery fragments (each with own delimiters, as D23 line 23). Fixtures: every alphabet x delimited/bare x wrapped/unwrapped x plain/zlib/hex inner, plus 5-byte Mastery fragments.\"},\n278\t  {\"id\": \"base92\", \"concept\": \"base92 (and base94/base95 printable-alphabet codecs)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Next size up after D23's 85 ('The alphabet got bigger'). base92 (thenoviceoof): alphabet '!' + '#'..'_' + 'a'..'}' (91 symbols, '~' = empty string), 13-bit pairs -> 2 chars, trailing 6-bit -> 1 char. chepy has from_base92 but ship a stdlib decoder in warmups_codecs (+ encoder for fixtures). Also base94 (all of '!'..'~') bignum and base95 (incl. space) via the bignum-radix-alphabets decoder. Cues: printable minus double-quote and backtick, ~1.23 x length, may end '~'. Fixtures: single blob + 5-byte Mastery fragments.\"},\n279\t  {\"id\": \"bignum-radix-alphabets\", \"concept\": \"whole text as ONE big integer in an arbitrary-radix alphabet (base94/95 printable, base85/91 bignum, base62/58 bignum, alphabet = sorted charset)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Generic catch-all for 'the alphabet got bigger' when no 4/5-chunk codec fits. For candidate alphabets (string.printable subsets: '!'..'~' (94), ' '..'~' (95), b85/a85/Z85/base91/base62/base58 alphabets, and ''.join(sorted(set(t)))), compute n = big-endian digit value, n.to_bytes(), also little-endian digit order; accept only UTF-8 text with the slug. Also leading-zero-symbol convention (base58 style). Cap at 2000 chars to stay < 50 ms. Fixtures: each alphabet x big/little digit order, single + fragment.\"},\n280\t  {\"id\": \"base65536\", \"concept\": \"base65536 / base32768 / base2048 (dense Unicode base-N)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"End of the 'bigger alphabet' road: 16 bits per CJK/Hangul-like BMP/astral char (base65536), 15 bits per char (base32768, UTF-16-friendly), 11 bits per char (base2048, tweet-sized). Ship stdlib decoders with the block tables embedded (base65536: 256 blocks of 256 code points + padding blocks; base32768/base2048: repertoire strings from the reference implementations) or guard chepy from_base65536 as an optional import. Cue: ~55-60 dense non-ASCII chars for a 110-byte sentence, no spaces. Fixtures: each codec, single + Mastery fragment.\"},\n281\t  {\"id\": \"mastery-line-routing\", \"concept\": \"Mastery: every day's codec must claim its RAW line inside decode_chunked / _joint_free\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery lost its first submit (113/113 sets: right slug words, wrong NN, every digit +5): the solver pre-decoded line 23 ('<~..~>' -> 'el-46') in place, and the joint free-codec search -- which has no identity option -- gave the plain line a digit ROT5. Rule: never rewrite numbered lines before decode_chunked; add the day's codec via register_free(name, day, fn) (gated to its own charset/delimiters) or decode_chunk. Before any timed start, print one set's joined sentence and check the slug digits against the single-solve shape. Same fields wrong on every set = one line's routing.\"},\n282\t  {\"id\": \"byte-family-mastery-cost\", \"concept\": \"Mastery solve time per set as codecs accumulate; lane-solver continuity\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D21 Mastery (103 x 21) died at the 60 s harness budget because solve.py was an ad-hoc generic per-line brute force, not the carried D20 lane solver; the D20 solver + one `_b64z` branch did 0.34 s. D22 Mastery (108 x 22) passed first try with the D21 solver unchanged (plus the solverrt partial-emit wrapper) but solve took 15.9 s and submit 11.8 s -- profile per set if it grows; D23 (113 x 23) solved in 1.2 s. Rule: copy the previous day's solve.py, add today's codec as one whole-blob step + register_free(name, day, fn), return early, time hctf solver-test on the real Mastery case before any timed start.\"},\n283\t  {\"id\": \"serialization-wrappers\", \"concept\": \"serialization formats as the wrapper: pickle, marshal, msgpack, BSON, CBOR, protobuf wire, Java serialization, PHP serialize, .NET BinaryFormatter\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Wrapper'/'package' puns. NEVER unpickle/deserialize untrusted bytes: use pickletools.genops / a tiny msgpack-CBOR-BSON-protobuf wire walker / regex for PHP 's:N:\\\"...\\\"' and Java TC_STRING (0x74 + u16 len) to pull out strings, then slug-gate (and run decode_chunk on each string). Cues: b64 'gASV'/'gAN' (pickle), 'rO0AB' (Java), 'AAEAAAD/////' (.NET), 0x82-0x8f/0xa0-0xbf leading bytes (msgpack map/str), BSON int32 length + 0x02 type. Retry: prebuild attempt 1 did not pass (ok=false); keep it stdlib-only, normal imports, no deserialization.\"},\n284\t  {\"id\": \"case-and-digit-loss\", \"concept\": \"case-losing / digit-losing codecs (Morse, NATO, Polybius, tap, Bacon, A1Z26, T9)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Output must be lowercased; A1Z26/Polybius/Bacon/tap have no digit symbols, so slug digits are passed through literally or spelled - the decoder must keep non-alphabet tokens verbatim. Lowercase only the FINAL text, and test a collapsed output for an inner hex/digit layer first (D16 Morse -> UPPERCASE hex, D17 Bacon -> a-p).\"},\n285\t  {\"id\": \"transposition-mastery-joint\", \"concept\": \"short Mastery fragments under a transposition (6-8 chars, key restarts per line)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D18 line 18 ('p-pr5e6' -> 'pper-56') has no charset cue; decode_chunked misses it (a D21 generalize worker's intermediate run left 'Master:i rbsk-...'). Keep the slug-gated per-line rail pass; register any future transposition decoder as a free codec with its day number so _joint_free tries it on each unclaimed line.\"},\n286\t  {\"id\": \"affine-free-strict\", \"concept\": \"affine as a GM-confirmed-ready free codec\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Already prebuilt (wc:affine + SPECULATIVE_FREE + _fit_affine). Risk is only bigram ranking vs rot-N/Atbash in Mastery joint assignment; confirm ratchet path registers it with a day number on first sight.\"},\n287\t  {\"id\": \"chepy-cyberchef-cue\", \"concept\": \"standard-tool fallback for any unseen encoding\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"chepy (venv) has from_base45/58/62/85/91/92/65536, rot_8000, from_upside_down, decode_zero_width, from_fullwidth, from_bacon, from_braille, from_nato, sms_decode_multitap, vigenere_decode, bifid_decode, gzip/zlib/bzip/lzma/lz4/lz77 _decompress, raw_inflate, unzip_all, tar_extract_all; CyberChef ops at tools/npm-cyberchef/node_modules/cyberchef/src/core/operations (Magic recipe finds compression layers).\"},\n288\t  {\"id\": \"base256-glyph-bytes\", \"concept\": \"one glyph per byte from a 256-symbol set: Braille U+2800+byte, base256emoji, cp437/Latin-1 printable maps, U+0100+byte offset blocks\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Alphabet as big as a byte'. Detect: every char non-ASCII and in ONE contiguous block (or the base256emoji table), count == 105-115. Decode: bytes(ord(c) - block_start) when all fall in a 256-wide window; base256emoji via its published 256-emoji table; cp437 via bytes(t.encode('cp437')) reversal. Then UTF-8 + slug gate, else feed bytes back to decode_chunk (inner layer). Fixtures: Braille-bytes, U+0100 offset, base256emoji, cp437.\"},\n289\t  {\"id\": \"base122-dense-utf8\", \"concept\": \"base122 (7-bit packing into UTF-8 with 2-byte illegal-char escapes) and similar dense UTF-8 packings\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Base-122 (kevinAlbs): 7-bit groups as 1-byte UTF-8; the 6 'illegal' values (0, 10, 13, 34, 38, 92) go into 2-byte 110sssxx 10xxxxxx sequences with the next 7 bits. Ship a stdlib decoder + encoder. Cue: valid UTF-8 mixing ASCII control-free text with \\\\xc2-\\\\xdf lead bytes, ~1.14 x the byte length, artifact may be bytes not text (read raw). Fixtures: single + fragment.\"},\n290\t  {\"id\": \"bech32-base58check\", \"concept\": \"checksummed base-N encodings: base58check, bech32 / bech32m, Ripple / Flickr base58 alphabets\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Crypto-address dress for base-N. bech32: 'hrp' + '1' + data in 'qpzry9x8gf2tvdw0s3jn54khce6mua7l' (5-bit), last 6 chars checksum -> regroup 5->8 bits (drop padding); verify polymod with const 1 (bech32) or 0x2bc830a3 (bech32m). base58check: base58 decode, strip 1 version byte + 4 checksum bytes (sha256d). Ripple alphabet 'rpshnaf39wBUDNEGHJKLM4PQRST7VWXYZ2bcdeCg65jkm8oFqi1tuvAxyz', Flickr = lowercase-first. Fixtures for each, crib-gated.\"},\n291\t  {\"id\": \"zalgo-combining-strip\", \"concept\": \"zalgo / combining-mark noise and NFD-decomposed text\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Strip unicodedata.combining() > 0 after NFD; then the normal pipeline. Cue: base letters buried under stacked U+0300-036F marks. Tiny decoder + fixture; register in CANDIDATES. Retry: prebuild attempt 1 did not pass (ok=false).\"},\n292\t  {\"id\": \"middle-endian-pdp\", \"concept\": \"middle-endian / PDP-11 byte order (2143, 3412) for 32-bit words: UTF-32 or u32 char codes\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Given up after 2 prebuild attempts (attempt 1 failed the lib lint: '__import__() not allowed'). Byte-order family closed at D20; if a PDP/middle-endian day ever comes: try all 24 permutations of each 4-byte word, then utf-32-be / utf-16-be, crib-gated; a permuted BOM (00 00 fe ff -> fe ff 00 00 ...) is the cue.\"},\n293\t  {\"id\": \"bifid-adfgvx\", \"concept\": \"Bifid / Trifid / ADFGX / ADFGVX / Nihilist\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"pycipher implements all; key from title; ADFGX cue is the 5/6-letter alphabet.\"},\n294\t  {\"id\": \"mime-encoded-word\", \"concept\": \"MIME encoded-word headers\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"email.header.decode_header handles =?charset?B|Q?...?=. Body-level MIME wrappers are in text-armor-wrappers.\"},\n295\t  {\"id\": \"esoteric\", \"concept\": \"Brainfuck / Ook! (Chuck Norris unary is prebuilt: chuck_dec)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"No bf interpreter installed; a 20-line stdlib interpreter or pip 'brainfuck-interpreter' if one ever appears.\"},\n296\t  {\"id\": \"misc-tables\", \"concept\": \"chemical symbols, Cetacean, Citrix CTX1 (DNA/codon, Roman, BCD, Gray, Kenny are prebuilt in warmups_codecs)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Recognition cues only; each is a lookup table the worker can write in one turn; CyberChef has From BCD and Cetacean Cipher Decode.\"},\n297\t  {\"id\": \"homoglyph\", \"concept\": \"homoglyph (Cyrillic/Greek look-alike) substitution\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"unidecode/confusables not installed; NFKC does not fold Cyrillic. Install unidecode only if a day uses it.\"}\n298\t]\n299\t```\n300\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57a499fe-6ce0-43d7-8cfd-6fceb5b2390a","uuid":"7ab3b77f-d200-4306-a564-911afe3bef6e","timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:21:30.133Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/warmups.md","content":"| 154 | git loose objects / other inflate-then-header containers: zlib of `blob <len>\\0<text>` (also `tree`/`commit`), PNG `zTXt`/`iTXt`, HTTP chunked + `Content-Encoding: gzip` | prebuilt tgt:inflate-container-headers | yes | inflated text starts `blob 110\\0`; `IHDR`/`zTXt`; `HTTP/1.1` + `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` | strip the container header (`split(b'\\0',1)[1]`), de-chunk hex sizes, then decompress/decode | med: knob on D22 (same zlib, different payload) |\n| 155 | yEnc / BinHex 4.0 / Ascii85-with-`<~~>` armor variants | prebuilt tgt:yenc-binhex | yes | `=ybegin line=128 size=..`; `(This file must be converted with BinHex 4.0)` + `:...:` | yEnc: `(b-42-64*esc)%256`; BinHex: RLE90 + hqx (binascii hqx removed in 3.11 -> small decoder) | low-med: retro binary-to-text |\n| 156 | zalgo / combining-mark noise over the sentence (U+0300-036F stacked), or decomposed NFD text | gap (gap zalgo-combining-strip) | yes | letters with many combining diacritics; `unicodedata.combining(c)` > 0 | `''.join(c for c in unicodedata.normalize('NFD',t) if not unicodedata.combining(c))` | low |\n| 157 | Ascii85 knobs / other 85-alphabets: no `<~ ~>`, `z` (4 NULs) and `y` (4 spaces) shortcuts, line-wrapped at 75/76/80, whitespace inside, btoa (`xbtoa Begin` ... `xbtoa End N n E S R` trailer), RFC1924/git/Python `b85` (0-9A-Za-z + 23 symbols; no quotes, comma, dot, slash, colon, brackets, backslash), Z85, IPv6 RFC1924 (20-char address), a85 over a seen inner layer (hex/UTF-16/gzip/zlib) | gap (gap base85-variant-sweep) | yes | charset of 85 printables; delimiters/trailer; length%5 in {0,2,3,4}; Z85 has `.` `:` `[` `]` and no `,` `;` `_` | `a85decode(t, adobe=..)`, `b85decode`, Z85 via `str.translate` to the b85 alphabet then `b85decode`; btoa = a85 per line, check the trailer; then magic sniff + `decode_chunk` | high: D24 knob on D23 |\n| 158 | whole text as ONE big integer in an arbitrary radix alphabet (base94 `!`-`~`, base95 incl. space, base85/91 as bignum, base62/58 bignum, alphabet = sorted charset) | gap (gap bignum-radix-alphabets) | yes | printable soup with no 4/5-chunk structure; length ~ 110*8/log2(N) | `n = sum(i*N**k)`; `n.to_bytes((n.bit_length()+7)//8,'big')`; try sorted(set(t)) and the standard alphabets; crib gate | med: \"bigger alphabet\" generalised |\n| 159 | base122 / other dense UTF-8 byte packings (7 bits per byte, 2-byte \"illegal\" sequences) | gap (gap base122-dense-utf8) | yes | valid UTF-8 mixing ASCII with `\\xc2`-`\\xdf` two-byte chars, ~1.14 x length | spec decoder (strip high bits, re-pack 7-bit groups) | low-med |\n| 160 | 256-glyph byte maps: one glyph per byte (Braille U+2800+byte, base256emoji (multiformats), cp437 / Latin-1 printable map, `U+0100+byte`) | gap (gap base256-glyph-bytes) | yes | non-ASCII glyphs from ONE block, count = text length (110-115) | `bytes(ord(c)-base for c in t)` / table lookup | med: \"alphabet as big as a byte\" |\n| 161 | checksummed base-N: base58check (version byte + 4-byte SHA-256d checksum), bech32/bech32m (`hrp1` + `qpzry9x8gf2tvdw0s3jn54khce6mua7l` 5-bit groups + 6-char checksum), Ripple/Flickr base58 alphabets | gap (gap bech32-base58check) | yes | `bc1`/`hrp1` prefix, the bech32 charset; base58 with leading `1`s | regroup 5->8 bits after dropping hrp + checksum; base58 decode then strip version/checksum | low-med |\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\nKnown plaintext: \"Nice work decoding this warmup! To solve, submit this exact answer to the Game Master: a-b-c-NN\"\n word lengths: 4 4 8 4 6! 2 5, 6 4 5 6 2 3 4 6: slug   (exactly one \"!\", one \",\", one \":\")\n crib letters cover all but f j q y z; slug is ALWAYS lowercase -> lowercase case-losing decodes before submit\nSTEP 1 - lib first: python3 -c \"from lib import decode,warmups_codecs as w;t=open('blob.txt').read();\n  print(decode.decode_chunk(t)); print([n for n,e,d in w.CANDIDATES if d and w.SLUG.search(w.safe(d,t.strip()) or '')])\"\nSTEP 2 - charset fingerprint (python: sorted(set(t)), len(t), len(t)/110):\n [01] 8/7-groups .................. binary (D4); 4-groups -> nibbles->hex; 5-groups -> Bacon/Baudot; 0-blocks -> Chuck Norris\n [0-7] 3-digit ................... octal (D6);   [0-9] 32-126 tokens -> decimal (D5); 1-26 dashed -> A1Z26\n ONE long digit run, no spaces .... whole text as a big integer (to_bytes big/little); 4-10 digit tokens -> u16/u32 words\n digit pairs 1-5 -> Polybius/tap code (. or x knocks too);  runs of 2-9 repeats -> multitap (44 33 555); 2-9 singles -> T9\n [0-9a-f] even, x2 ................ hex (D3); c1-e9/81-a9 + 40 -> EBCDIC cp037\n hex x4 starting fffe (D19 LE 4e00) / feff (D20 BE 004e), 00 every 2nd byte = UTF-16: .decode('utf-16') takes EITHER BOM;\n   fffe0000/0000feff -> UTF-32; NULs in a non-LE/BE 4-byte pattern -> middle-endian; d8xx dcxx -> surrogates, then NFKC;\n   pairs/quads swapped -> byte-swap words; base64 with AG/AA rhythm -> b64 then utf-16-le; LSB-first bits\n . - only (+ / or 3 spaces) ....... Morse (D16: output only 0-9A-F -> hex layer; digits -> char codes); 1/111 runs -> timing\n a/b (A/B) in 5s .................. Baconian (D17: all groups start `a` -> values 0-15 = HEX nibbles, 2 per byte);\n                                    values up to 25 -> letters; odd casing in cover text -> Bacon via case\n ANY 16-symbol output (0-9A-F, a-p only, 16 words) after a carrier = hex nibbles -> fromhex (D16, D17);\n   unknown 16 tokens -> map them by the crib hex `4e 69 63 65 20 77 6f 72 6b`. lib: twosym/bin4/aphex/tern/radix_dec\n 2-symbol groups of width 5/6 with values >15 -> base32/base64 INDEX;  ䷀.. hexagrams -> base64;  only space/TAB -> bits\n dotted quads/#RRGGBB/4e69:6365 -> IPv4/colour/IPv6 bytes; b64-ish won't decode -> undo rev/rot13 1st (U4fV=rot13 H4sI)\n ADFGX(V) only -> ADFGVX (key: title word + crib);  A C G T only -> DNA 2-bit / codon\n %XX .............................. URL (D7);  &#..; -> HTML (D8);  \\uXXXX -> JSON (D9);  \\xNN -> C escape\n U+XXXX / %uXXXX / \\U0000XXXX -> chr(int(h,16));  =XX / soft \"=\\n\" -> quoted-printable;  =?UTF-8?B?..?= -> MIME\n A-Z2-7 (=) ....................... base32 (D10);  0-9A-V -> base32hex;  ybndrfg8.. -> z-base-32;  no ILOU -> Crockford\n A-Za-z0-9+/ (=), len%4==0 ........ base64 (D1); H4sI = GZIP inside (D21: base64 -d | gzip -dc); eN = ZLIB 78da (D22:\n   zlib.decompress(b64decode(t)); eJ/eF/eA other levels; zlib = (b0<<8|b1)%31==0, not just 0x78; no magic -> wbits=-15);\n   Qlpo bz2, /Td6WFo xz, KLUv/ zstd, UEsDB zip, N3q8 7z, U2FsdGVkX1 openssl, .eJ flask cookie, eyJ JWT -> never score bytes\n A-Za-z0-9-_ no = ................. base64url (D11);  [0-9A-Za-z] only, no pad -> base62 (x1.34) / base36 one case (x1.55)\n no 0 O I l + / = -> base58 (x1.37);  0-9A-Z plus space $%*+-./: -> base45 (x1.5)\n <~ ... ~> around ! .. u ......... ASCII85 (D23): a85decode(t,adobe=True); no <~ -> a85decode (z = 4 NULs);\n   RFC1924 set (no quotes , . / : [ \\ ]) -> b85decode; .-:+=^!/*?&<>()[]{}@%$# -> Z85; xbtoa Begin -> btoa\n ~all printable, no ' - \\ ......... basE91 (x1.23);  ! .. } minus \" ` -> base92;  no chunk structure -> bignum radix\n begin 644 / lines start M or h ... uuencode / xxencode;  xn-- labels -> punycode/IDNA\nNON-ASCII:\n U+2800-28FF ⠝⠊⠉⠑ ................. Braille (⠼ = number sign)\n fullwidth Ｎｉｃｅ / math 𝐍𝐢𝐜𝐞 / ⓝ .. NFKC normalize\n ɐ q ɔ p ǝ ɟ ƃ ɥ ᴉ ʞ ɯ ɹ ʇ ʌ ʍ ʎ ...... upside-down (chepy from_upside_down, then maybe [::-1])\n CJK U+7Cxx, spaces kept -> ROT8000;  dense CJK/Hangul -> base65536/2048;  emoji 1/byte -> base100;  CJK U+xx00 -> swap bytes\n invisible U+200B/C/D/2060/FEFF -> zero-width stego;  ASCII-looking with odd bytes -> homoglyphs (Cyrillic)\nSAME LENGTH, LETTERS ONLY CHANGE (word lengths 4 4 8 4 6! ... kept):\n best rot-N English -> Caesar (D2 rot13, D14 +7); digits also +5 -> ROT18/ROT5;  mirror a<->z -> Atbash (D13)\n crib c-p constant ratio .......... affine (lib _fit_affine); constant per position mod k -> Vigenere key = (c-p)\n crib c+p periodic -> Beaufort (primer then plaintext -> autokey);  crib map consistent, not affine -> keyword subst\n neighbour keys (Muvr eptl) ....... QWERTY shift;  ;,.' in words -> Dvorak;  ALL printables shift -> ROT47 (D15)/ROT8000\nSAME CHARACTER MULTISET (anagram: one ! , :, slug digits intact) = TRANSPOSITION (D12 reverse, D18 rail 3):\n rail fence (D18: number in prompt = rails; w.rail_solve) | redefence | scytale/columnar (w.col_solve) | route/Caesar box\n | skip k | riffle | word order. Strip only \\r\\n (spaces are ciphertext); accept only text STARTING `Nice work`\nWORDS: Alfa Bravo -> NATO; -ay -> Pig Latin; N1c3 w0rk -> leet. Title pun -> key: cipher + number = key (D18 \"Three rails\")\n\"Same ...\"/\"Another ...\"/\"This time ...\" (D20, D22) = yesterday's codec, ONE knob turned; \"alphabet got bigger\" (D23) = base-N size\nMastery: line k = day k's codec; keyed/transposed lines restart the key PER LINE (D18: 6-8 char rail-3 slug tail);\n lines 19/20 own BOM (LE+BE in one blob), 21/22 own gzip/zlib streams, 23 own `<~..~>`. NEVER pre-decode a line in place\n before decode_chunked (D23: plain `el-46` got ROT5 -> all 113 NN wrong) -- register_free(name, day, fn) instead.\n STACKS (D16-17, D19-21): output hex/digits/b32/a-p/NUL-rhythm/compressed-magic bytes -> decode AGAIN. Solver: return on the first full slug; slow fallbacks only on a miss.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"base85-variant-sweep\", \"concept\": \"Ascii85 knobs and the other 85-character alphabets: no delimiters, z/y shortcuts, wrapped lines, btoa, RFC1924/git b85, Z85, IPv6 RFC1924, a85 over a seen inner layer\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Most likely D24 (knob on D23 Adobe Ascii85 '<~...~>'). Build warmups_codecs.b85_any(t): strip whitespace/newlines; '<~..~>' -> a85decode(adobe=True) (append '~>' if only '<~' present); else a85decode(t) (z = 4 NULs) and a85decode(t, foldspaces=True) (y); b85decode (RFC1924/git/Python alphabet); Z85 via str.translate(Z85 alphabet -> b85 alphabet) then b85decode (pad to len%5==0 only for b85-style partials); btoa: lines between 'xbtoa Begin' and 'xbtoa End', a85 per line; IPv6 RFC1924 = 20-char token -> 16 bytes. Then magic sniff (gzip/zlib/bz2/xz/raw deflate) and decode_chunk on the output (hex/UTF-16/base64 inner layers), slug-gated. Register as a whole-blob candidate AND a free codec for 7-12 char Mastery fragments (each with own delimiters, as D23 line 23). Fixtures: every alphabet x delimited/bare x wrapped/unwrapped x plain/zlib/hex inner, plus 5-byte Mastery fragments.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"base92\", \"concept\": \"base92 (and base94/base95 printable-alphabet codecs)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Next size up after D23's 85 ('The alphabet got bigger'). base92 (thenoviceoof): alphabet '!' + '#'..'_' + 'a'..'}' (91 symbols, '~' = empty string), 13-bit pairs -> 2 chars, trailing 6-bit -> 1 char. chepy has from_base92 but ship a stdlib decoder in warmups_codecs (+ encoder for fixtures). Also base94 (all of '!'..'~') bignum and base95 (incl. space) via the bignum-radix-alphabets decoder. Cues: printable minus double-quote and backtick, ~1.23 x length, may end '~'. Fixtures: single blob + 5-byte Mastery fragments.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bignum-radix-alphabets\", \"concept\": \"whole text as ONE big integer in an arbitrary-radix alphabet (base94/95 printable, base85/91 bignum, base62/58 bignum, alphabet = sorted charset)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Generic catch-all for 'the alphabet got bigger' when no 4/5-chunk codec fits. For candidate alphabets (string.printable subsets: '!'..'~' (94), ' '..'~' (95), b85/a85/Z85/base91/base62/base58 alphabets, and ''.join(sorted(set(t)))), compute n = big-endian digit value, n.to_bytes(), also little-endian digit order; accept only UTF-8 text with the slug. Also leading-zero-symbol convention (base58 style). Cap at 2000 chars to stay < 50 ms. Fixtures: each alphabet x big/little digit order, single + fragment.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"base65536\", \"concept\": \"base65536 / base32768 / base2048 (dense Unicode base-N)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"End of the 'bigger alphabet' road: 16 bits per CJK/Hangul-like BMP/astral char (base65536), 15 bits per char (base32768, UTF-16-friendly), 11 bits per char (base2048, tweet-sized). Ship stdlib decoders with the block tables embedded (base65536: 256 blocks of 256 code points + padding blocks; base32768/base2048: repertoire strings from the reference implementations) or guard chepy from_base65536 as an optional import. Cue: ~55-60 dense non-ASCII chars for a 110-byte sentence, no spaces. Fixtures: each codec, single + Mastery fragment.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-line-routing\", \"concept\": \"Mastery: every day's codec must claim its RAW line inside decode_chunked / _joint_free\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery lost its first submit (113/113 sets: right slug words, wrong NN, every digit +5): the solver pre-decoded line 23 ('<~..~>' -> 'el-46') in place, and the joint free-codec search -- which has no identity option -- gave the plain line a digit ROT5. Rule: never rewrite numbered lines before decode_chunked; add the day's codec via register_free(name, day, fn) (gated to its own charset/delimiters) or decode_chunk. Before any timed start, print one set's joined sentence and check the slug digits against the single-solve shape. Same fields wrong on every set = one line's routing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"byte-family-mastery-cost\", \"concept\": \"Mastery solve time per set as codecs accumulate; lane-solver continuity\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D21 Mastery (103 x 21) died at the 60 s harness budget because solve.py was an ad-hoc generic per-line brute force, not the carried D20 lane solver; the D20 solver + one `_b64z` branch did 0.34 s. D22 Mastery (108 x 22) passed first try with the D21 solver unchanged (plus the solverrt partial-emit wrapper) but solve took 15.9 s and submit 11.8 s -- profile per set if it grows; D23 (113 x 23) solved in 1.2 s. Rule: copy the previous day's solve.py, add today's codec as one whole-blob step + register_free(name, day, fn), return early, time hctf solver-test on the real Mastery case before any timed start.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"serialization-wrappers\", \"concept\": \"serialization formats as the wrapper: pickle, marshal, msgpack, BSON, CBOR, protobuf wire, Java serialization, PHP serialize, .NET BinaryFormatter\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Wrapper'/'package' puns. NEVER unpickle/deserialize untrusted bytes: use pickletools.genops / a tiny msgpack-CBOR-BSON-protobuf wire walker / regex for PHP 's:N:\\\"...\\\"' and Java TC_STRING (0x74 + u16 len) to pull out strings, then slug-gate (and run decode_chunk on each string). Cues: b64 'gASV'/'gAN' (pickle), 'rO0AB' (Java), 'AAEAAAD/////' (.NET), 0x82-0x8f/0xa0-0xbf leading bytes (msgpack map/str), BSON int32 length + 0x02 type. Retry: prebuild attempt 1 did not pass (ok=false); keep it stdlib-only, normal imports, no deserialization.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"case-and-digit-loss\", \"concept\": \"case-losing / digit-losing codecs (Morse, NATO, Polybius, tap, Bacon, A1Z26, T9)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Output must be lowercased; A1Z26/Polybius/Bacon/tap have no digit symbols, so slug digits are passed through literally or spelled - the decoder must keep non-alphabet tokens verbatim. Lowercase only the FINAL text, and test a collapsed output for an inner hex/digit layer first (D16 Morse -> UPPERCASE hex, D17 Bacon -> a-p).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"transposition-mastery-joint\", \"concept\": \"short Mastery fragments under a transposition (6-8 chars, key restarts per line)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D18 line 18 ('p-pr5e6' -> 'pper-56') has no charset cue; decode_chunked misses it (a D21 generalize worker's intermediate run left 'Master:i rbsk-...'). Keep the slug-gated per-line rail pass; register any future transposition decoder as a free codec with its day number so _joint_free tries it on each unclaimed line.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"affine-free-strict\", \"concept\": \"affine as a GM-confirmed-ready free codec\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Already prebuilt (wc:affine + SPECULATIVE_FREE + _fit_affine). Risk is only bigram ranking vs rot-N/Atbash in Mastery joint assignment; confirm ratchet path registers it with a day number on first sight.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"chepy-cyberchef-cue\", \"concept\": \"standard-tool fallback for any unseen encoding\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"chepy (venv) has from_base45/58/62/85/91/92/65536, rot_8000, from_upside_down, decode_zero_width, from_fullwidth, from_bacon, from_braille, from_nato, sms_decode_multitap, vigenere_decode, bifid_decode, gzip/zlib/bzip/lzma/lz4/lz77 _decompress, raw_inflate, unzip_all, tar_extract_all; CyberChef ops at tools/npm-cyberchef/node_modules/cyberchef/src/core/operations (Magic recipe finds compression layers).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"base256-glyph-bytes\", \"concept\": \"one glyph per byte from a 256-symbol set: Braille U+2800+byte, base256emoji, cp437/Latin-1 printable maps, U+0100+byte offset blocks\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"'Alphabet as big as a byte'. Detect: every char non-ASCII and in ONE contiguous block (or the base256emoji table), count == 105-115. Decode: bytes(ord(c) - block_start) when all fall in a 256-wide window; base256emoji via its published 256-emoji table; cp437 via bytes(t.encode('cp437')) reversal. Then UTF-8 + slug gate, else feed bytes back to decode_chunk (inner layer). Fixtures: Braille-bytes, U+0100 offset, base256emoji, cp437.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"base122-dense-utf8\", \"concept\": \"base122 (7-bit packing into UTF-8 with 2-byte illegal-char escapes) and similar dense UTF-8 packings\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Base-122 (kevinAlbs): 7-bit groups as 1-byte UTF-8; the 6 'illegal' values (0, 10, 13, 34, 38, 92) go into 2-byte 110sssxx 10xxxxxx sequences with the next 7 bits. Ship a stdlib decoder + encoder. Cue: valid UTF-8 mixing ASCII control-free text with \\\\xc2-\\\\xdf lead bytes, ~1.14 x the byte length, artifact may be bytes not text (read raw). Fixtures: single + fragment.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bech32-base58check\", \"concept\": \"checksummed base-N encodings: base58check, bech32 / bech32m, Ripple / Flickr base58 alphabets\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Crypto-address dress for base-N. bech32: 'hrp' + '1' + data in 'qpzry9x8gf2tvdw0s3jn54khce6mua7l' (5-bit), last 6 chars checksum -> regroup 5->8 bits (drop padding); verify polymod with const 1 (bech32) or 0x2bc830a3 (bech32m). base58check: base58 decode, strip 1 version byte + 4 checksum bytes (sha256d). Ripple alphabet 'rpshnaf39wBUDNEGHJKLM4PQRST7VWXYZ2bcdeCg65jkm8oFqi1tuvAxyz', Flickr = lowercase-first. Fixtures for each, crib-gated.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"zalgo-combining-strip\", \"concept\": \"zalgo / combining-mark noise and NFD-decomposed text\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Strip unicodedata.combining() > 0 after NFD; then the normal pipeline. Cue: base letters buried under stacked U+0300-036F marks. Tiny decoder + fixture; register in CANDIDATES. Retry: prebuild attempt 1 did not pass (ok=false).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"middle-endian-pdp\", \"concept\": \"middle-endian / PDP-11 byte order (2143, 3412) for 32-bit words: UTF-32 or u32 char codes\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Given up after 2 prebuild attempts (attempt 1 failed the lib lint: '__import__() not allowed'). Byte-order family closed at D20; if a PDP/middle-endian day ever comes: try all 24 permutations of each 4-byte word, then utf-32-be / utf-16-be, crib-gated; a permuted BOM (00 00 fe ff -> fe ff 00 00 ...) is the cue.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bifid-adfgvx\", \"concept\": \"Bifid / Trifid / ADFGX / ADFGVX / Nihilist\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"pycipher implements all; key from title; ADFGX cue is the 5/6-letter alphabet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mime-encoded-word\", \"concept\": \"MIME encoded-word headers\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"email.header.decode_header handles =?charset?B|Q?...?=. Body-level MIME wrappers are in text-armor-wrappers.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"esoteric\", \"concept\": \"Brainfuck / Ook! (Chuck Norris unary is prebuilt: chuck_dec)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"No bf interpreter installed; a 20-line stdlib interpreter or pip 'brainfuck-interpreter' if one ever appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"misc-tables\", \"concept\": \"chemical symbols, Cetacean, Citrix CTX1 (DNA/codon, Roman, BCD, Gray, Kenny are prebuilt in warmups_codecs)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Recognition cues only; each is a lookup table the worker can write in one turn; CyberChef has From BCD and Cetacean Cipher Decode.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"homoglyph\", \"concept\": \"homoglyph (Cyrillic/Greek look-alike) substitution\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"unidecode/confusables not installed; NFKC does not fold Cyrillic. Install unidecode only if a day uses it.\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":96,"startLine":205,"totalLines":300}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HsUQTndwzqp1YMib6sUZHV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
