value strings in order); sexp '(' ')' lists with optional '[display-hint]', transport forms {b64 of canonical} |b64 atom| #hex atom#. Join string leaves; slug-gate. Fixtures: bencoded list of 1-char strings, one long string, dict, canonical sexp, transport {..} form.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"length-prefix-binary-tlv\", \"concept\": \"binary length prefixes under hex/base64: Pascal strings, u16/u32 BE/LE lengths, varint (protobuf string field), TLV (type+len+value), hex-digit lengths\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n     \"detail\": \"Framing x the byte family (D19-D22 had byte-level knobs). After any hex/b64 decode, try: 1-byte len frames; 2/4-byte BE/LE len; LEB128 varint len (lib has LEB128); 1-byte type + 1/2-byte len (TLV); protobuf wire (tag byte 0x0a etc. + varint len); hex-digit len text frames ('0e' + data). Whole stream must parse; join payloads; slug-gate. Fixtures: one char per frame and one frame per word, each width/endianness, TLV with alternating type bytes, decoys (plain hex of text).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"string-builder-literals\", \"concept\": \"'String' as code: concatenated string literals, String.fromCharCode / chr() calls, char arrays, ''.join([...]), JSON/Python lists of characters\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n     \"detail\": \"Title-pun sibling of D24 ('String Theory'). Never eval: regex/ast.literal_eval only on literal-only nodes. Forms: \\\"Ni\\\" + \\\"ce\\\" (JS/Java/C#), Python implicit 'N' 'i', String.fromCharCode(78,105,...), chr(78)+chr(105), new char[]{'N','i'}, [char]78+[char]105 (PowerShell), ''.join(['N','i']), [\\\"N\\\",\\\"i\\\"] JSON, b'\\\\x4e' bytes literals. Extract literal pieces in order, unescape, join; slug-gate. Overlaps lib.scripts deobfuscators -- reuse them. Fixtures per language + decoys.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"resp-redis\", \"concept\": \"RESP (Redis serialization protocol) bulk/simple strings and arrays\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n     \"detail\": \"Length-prefixed 'string protocol' sibling: '*<n>\\\\r\\\\n' arrays, '$<len>\\\\r\\\\n<data>\\\\r\\\\n' bulk strings, '+text\\\\r\\\\n', ':int\\\\r\\\\n', RESP3 '=' verbatim. Cursor parser tolerant to bare '\\\\n'; join bulk strings; slug-gate. Fixtures: array of 1-char bulk strings, one bulk string per word, CRLF vs LF.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"http-chunked-transfer\", \"concept\": \"HTTP/1.1 chunked transfer encoding as a text framing (hex chunk sizes, CRLF, final 0 chunk, chunk extensions)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n     \"detail\": \"Framing with HEX lengths ('Count carefully' in base 16). Parser: read hex size up to ';' or CRLF, take size bytes, expect CRLF, loop until size 0; tolerate LF-only and missing trailer. Optionally Content-Encoding gzip/deflate on the dechunked body (reuse magic sniff). Fixtures: 1-char chunks, word chunks, extensions, gzip body.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"asn1-der-tlv\", \"concept\": \"ASN.1 DER/BER TLV strings (UTF8String 0c, OCTET STRING 04, PrintableString 13, IA5String 16, SEQUENCE 30) in hex/base64/PEM\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n     \"detail\": \"Standard TLV framing. Minimal stdlib walker: tag byte, short/long-form length, recurse into constructed (0x20 bit) types, collect string leaves in order, join; slug-gate. Cues: hex '30 81'/'30 82'/'0c'+len, base64 'MI'/'MD'/'DA'. asn1crypto may not be importable in the solver -- keep it stdlib. Fixtures: SEQUENCE of 1-char UTF8Strings, one OCTET STRING, BER indefinite length.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"delimited-field-framing\", \"concept\": \"CSV/TSV quoted fields with doubled-quote escapes, Lisp char lists, YAML flow sequences carrying one char or word per field\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n     \"detail\": \"Delimiter-escaping sibling of netstrings (the payload contains the delimiter, escaped instead of counted). csv.reader for '\\\"N\\\",\\\"i\\\",\\\"\\\"\\\"\\\"' (doubled quote), TSV with \\\\t escapes, Scheme #\\\\N char literals, YAML flow [N, i, ' ']. Join fields; slug-gate. Fixtures each + decoys.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"rhythm-broken-structure-first\", \"concept\": \"when the day is a NEW family with no charset fingerprint, read the blob's structure first\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\",\n     \"detail\": \"D24 broke the D19-D23 'new family, then one knob' rhythm (no Ascii85 knob; framing instead), and nothing prebuilt covered it. Worker rule: if STEP 1 (lib) misses, describe the repeating unit (here '\\\\d+:.,' x 111) and name the spec from it + the title pun before brute-forcing codecs; write a strict whole-text parser that returns None on mismatch so it can sit first in the pipeline.\"},\n]\nids = {g[\"id\"] for g in gaps}\nassert not ids & {g[\"id\"] for g in new}\np1 = [g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"] == 1]\nrest = [g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"] != 1]\ngaps = [g for g in new if g[\"priority\"] == 1] + p1 + [g for g in new if g[\"priority\"] == 2] + rest + [g for g in new if g[\"priority\"] == 3]\ngaps.sort(key=lambda g: g[\"priority\"])\nout = \"\\n[\\n\" + \",\\n\".join(\"  \" + json.dumps(g, ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps) + \"\\n]\\n\"\njson.loads(out)\ns = s[:j0] + out + s[j1:]\nopen(p, 'w').write(s)\nprint(len(gaps), sum(1 for g in gaps if g[\"action\"] == \"prebuild\"))\n"}}}
