{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgM8w6MToir1uUWVkswbS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated both warmups files for day 24, \"String Theory\". I changed nothing else and ran no tests or Game Master modes. The technique log is 233 lines, still over the ~200 target.\n\n1. **`reference/techniques/warmups.md`:**\n   - **Day 24 entry:** the blob was netstrings, the `<len>:<data>,` format. Each frame held one character (`1:N,1:i,...`), 444 bytes in all. The sentence's own `,` and `:` sit inside frames as data (`1:,,`, `1::,`), so it can only be parsed by counting lengths, not by splitting on commas. Single solve was CORRECT in about 30 s. Time trial (4.6 s) and Mastery (118 sets × 24 lines, 4.5 s) were both CORRECT on the first try. The slug was accepted exactly as decoded.\n   - **Other sections:** I added a \"Framing / length prefix\" variant axis, a recognition-cue row and a pitfall about never splitting on `,`.\n   - **Lane pattern:** the log now records that day 24 broke the \"new family, then one tweak the next day\" rhythm. The expected Ascii85 follow-up never came.\n   - **Space:** I merged the day 23 entry into the days 14-23 summary and shortened the Ascii85 axis.\n2. **`reference/coverage/warmups.md`:**\n   - **New rows:** row 162 marks netstrings `seen D24`, and rows 163-172 cover likely follow-ups.\n   - **Updated rows:** rows that were built overnight (base92, base65536, serialization and others) now show `prebuilt`. I also lowered the odds of an Ascii85 follow-up.\n   - **Recognition cues:** I added a netstring line and stayed within 60 lines.\n3. **Readiness gaps:** every earlier `prebuild` gap had already been built, so I removed those and added 10 new ones that haven't been built. Five are priority 1:\n   - more netstring variations (longer chunks, byte counts, nesting)\n   - numbered frames out of order, or run-length counts\n   - tnetstrings\n   - bencode and S-expressions\n   - binary length prefixes and TLV\n\n   The other five are priority 2-3: RESP, HTTP chunked encoding, ASN.1 DER, strings built in code, and quoted CSV fields. I also added a priority-1 note telling workers to read the blob's structure first when there is no recognisable character set."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":365,"cache_read_input_tokens":116166,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":365},"output_tokens":792,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57a499fe-6ce0-43d7-8cfd-6fceb5b2390a","uuid":"10ea43fb-a679-4055-b048-377e16a34d82","timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:25:55.500Z","request_id":"req_011CgM8w5z8hyn7oTe77BiMc"}
